# Pin the INTERNAL Radeon Pro to its lowest power state. Never the eGPU.
# Managed by roles/linux; installed to /etc/udev/rules.d/30-amdgpu-pm.rules.
#
# This REPLACES a hand-written rule at the same path (dated 2026-05-20, owned by
# no package, undeclared anywhere in this repo) which read:
#
#   KERNEL=="card[012]", SUBSYSTEM=="drm", DRIVERS=="amdgpu", \
#     ATTR{device/power_dpm_force_performance_level}="low"
#
# The intent was thermal, and it is a reasonable intent on this machine: the
# 2018 15" chassis already pins the CPU package at 100 C with fans maxed under
# sustained load (see the Task 6 thermal baseline in
# specs/linux-migration/runbook.md), so holding the internal dGPU down is a
# sensible way to buy headroom on a host that mostly runs headless with the lid
# shut.
#
# The BUG was `card[012]`, which matches by /sys/class/drm card NUMBER. Those
# numbers are not stable here: the RX 580 eGPU has been card3 and is now card0,
# because dracut/amdgpu enumeration order changes when the Thunderbolt topology
# changes. So a rule written for the internal GPU silently clamped the eGPU too.
#
# The cost was not subtle. The eGPU sat locked at DPM level 0 -- 300 MHz core
# against a 1360 MHz maximum, and 300 MHz memory against 2000 MHz -- roughly
# 4.5x down on core and 6.7x down on bandwidth. Portal ran ON the RX 580 and was
# still slow, which is a genuinely confusing symptom: device selection was
# correct and the hardware was crippled anyway.
#
# The thermal argument also does not apply to the eGPU: it lives in a Razer Core
# with its own fan and its own power supply, outside the chassis whose heat this
# rule exists to manage.
#
# Matched on PCI vendor+device instead of card number, so it stays correct
# through any re-cabling or re-enumeration:
#   0x1002:0x67ef  Baffin / Polaris11  -- the internal Radeon Pro   -> clamped
#   0x1002:0x67df  Ellesmere / Polaris10 -- the RX 580 in the Core  -> untouched
ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="drm", KERNEL=="card*", \
  ATTRS{vendor}=="0x1002", ATTRS{device}=="0x67ef", \
  ATTR{device/power_dpm_force_performance_level}="low"
